      "id": 487952,
      "username": "peterg",
      "name": "Peter",
      "created_at": "2025-12-02T10:36:02.313Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Unless I’m mistaken, I don’t think you’ll be able to change base fields with just a json import. Base fields are manipulated with a Property Setter document. That’s what the Customize Form tool handles.</p>\n<p>If you want to create Property Setters programmatically, you’ll have to specify that as well. Fixtures would be one way to accomplish this.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/python-api/hooks#fixtures\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"/files/framework%20(1).png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" width=\"\" height=\"\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/python-api/hooks#fixtures\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">docs.frappe.io</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    \n\n<h3><a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/framework/user/en/python-api/hooks#fixtures\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hooks</a></h3>\n\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n",
